{"name":"Open Items","source":"Workpapers.xlsx","sha256":"34c29f6fcf6bf17f07ce8b77346432da13ecc2d009d6943682f29fb349b22c6e","kind":"workpaper","rows":[["HANGS Construction Services LLC",null,null,null,null],["Open Items",null,null,null,null],["Calendar year 2026 · USD · Form 940 · EIN 00-4567890 (demonstration) · fourth quarter projected",null,null,null,null],["DRAFT · NOT FOR FILING · human review required; a person signs and files",null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],["Reference","Status","Amount","Evidence or decision required",null],["CREDIT-01","OPEN","Missing evidence or decision","Washington is not on the 2025 credit reduction list (California 1.2%, the U.S. Virgin Islands 4.5%), and every HANGS wage is a Washington wage, so line 11 is $0.00 and no Schedule A is attached. The Department of Labor names the 2026 credit reduction states in November 2026, after the November 10 repayment deadline. A person checks the 2026 list before signing; each 0.3% of credit reduction would add $2,121.00 on $707,000.00 of FUTA wages, due with a fourth-quarter deposit by February 1, 2027.",null],["LABOR-01","OPEN",42,"Tomas Arvelo, an individual, was paid $21,168.00 through accounts payable in Q3 for 504 hours of concrete finishing at $42.00 an hour, working under the HGC foreman at Tideflats Cold Storage, and the client plans to send a Form 1099-NEC. Whether he is an employee is a common-law question for a person; the IRS can also be asked on Form SS-8. If he is, he gets a Form W-2 instead, $7,000.00 of FUTA wages and $42.00 of tax join Q3 (line 16c), and line 3 grows by $21,168.00. The draft reports the payroll as recorded.",null],["DEPOSIT-01","OPEN",81.12,"The Q1 FUTA deposit of $4,055.90 was due Thursday, April 30, 2026; the client's log shows it made Friday, May 1, 2026, 1 day late. The IRS may assess a 2% failure-to-deposit penalty, $81.12; a person decides whether to ask for relief if it does. Because not all FUTA tax was deposited when due, the return is due February 1, 2027, not February 10, 2027. Q2 and Q3 were carried forward correctly ($115.61 at September 30). The projected $186.10 undeposited at December 31 is $500 or less and may be paid with the return; a credit reduction (CREDIT-01) would put it over $500 and require a deposit by February 1, 2027.",null],["STATE-01","OPEN","Missing evidence or decision","The full 5.4% credit, with lines 9 and 10 at zero, assumes all 2026 Washington unemployment tax is paid by February 1, 2027. The Q2 ESD report as filed left out the June 26 bonus run ($55,500.00 of wages), the Q3 report was due November 2, 2026 and the Q4 report is due February 1, 2027. A person confirms the amended Q2 report and the Q3 and Q4 payments are made by then; state tax paid later limits the credit through the line 10 worksheet.",null],["Q4-01","OPEN","Missing evidence or decision","The fourth quarter is projected: October 2, 16 and 30 as paid; November 13 and 27, December 11 and December 24 at scheduled hours and current rates with no overtime; one planned hire, Alicia Castellano from November 16. FUTA changes only for employees still under $7,000: Yusuf Quintero, Alicia Castellano. Line 3, line 5 and line 16d ($70.49) are refreshed from the final December register in January before the return is signed.",null],["RETURN-01","OPEN","Missing evidence or decision","Unsigned draft. The 2026 return is due Monday, February 1, 2027 (January 31 is a Sunday); February 10, 2027 does not apply (DEPOSIT-01). A person reviews the open items, refreshes Q4, signs and files the return. Nothing has been filed or paid.",null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,nul